# Example ONLY — copy to /opt/circuits-com/.env on the MAIL box and fill in.
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy. Every value below is a placeholder.
#
#   sudo install -D -m 0600 /dev/null /opt/circuits-com/.env
#   sudo -e /opt/circuits-com/.env
#
# systemd reads this file verbatim (EnvironmentFile=): KEY=value, one per line,
# no `export`, and no inline comments after a value.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The shared bearer token. The SAME value goes in /opt/circuits-com/.env on the
# WEB box as MAIL_SYNC_SECRET, and nowhere else — not in git, not in the
# compose files, not in a chat message. The receiver refuses to start on
# anything shorter than 32 characters.
#
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
MAIL_SYNC_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-48-byte-urlsafe-token

# ── Optional (defaults shown) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# docker-mailserver's account list, on the host side of the `dms-config` Docker
# volume (named explicitly in mail/docker-compose.mail.yml). Verify the
# mountpoint on the box — it is not guaranteed to be this literal path:
#   docker volume inspect -f '{{.Mountpoint}}' dms-config
# If you change it, change ReadWritePaths= in circuits-mail-sync.service too.
#MAIL_SYNC_ACCOUNTS_FILE=/var/lib/docker/volumes/dms-config/_data/postfix-accounts.cf

# The closed allowlist of writable addresses. Keep it identical to the web
# box's MAIL_SYNC_MAILBOXES. `demo@` is a website login identity with no
# mailbox and must stay out of both lists.
#MAIL_SYNC_ALLOWED_ACCOUNTS=anthony@circuitcenter.ai,daniel@circuitcenter.ai,matthew@circuitcenter.ai,ronald@circuitcenter.ai,no-reply@circuitcenter.ai

# Listen address/port. The security group — not this — is what restricts
# callers to the web box's private IP.
#MAIL_SYNC_BIND=0.0.0.0
#MAIL_SYNC_PORT=8825

# Serve HTTPS. Set BOTH once mail.circuitcenter.ai has its Let's Encrypt
# certificate; the service logs a warning on every start until you do.
#MAIL_SYNC_TLS_CERT=/etc/letsencrypt/live/mail.circuitcenter.ai/fullchain.pem
#MAIL_SYNC_TLS_KEY=/etc/letsencrypt/live/mail.circuitcenter.ai/privkey.pem

# Explicit reload. Normally unnecessary: docker-mailserver's change detector
# picks the rewritten file up within seconds. Only set this if that detector is
# disabled — and then also uncomment the /run/docker.sock ReadWritePaths line
# in circuits-mail-sync.service.
#MAIL_SYNC_RELOAD_CMD=docker exec mailserver supervisorctl restart changedetector
